REFERENCE2 (24 colored stick figures) is a MOTION/PLACEMENT GUIDE ONLY. In each output cell, draw the SAME whole dragon girl in that cell's corresponding skeleton pose. Follow the elbow/wrist coordinates, eye-closing state and head angle in ALL24 cells. Red skeleton is her RIGHT arm on SCREEN LEFT. Blue is her other arm. These are not final graphic elements: do NOT render bones, dots, diagram colors, frame labels, grid lines or ground lines. Render complete natural bodies with connected shoulders/elbows/hands, covered by the unchanged dress and sleeves.
Layout exactly6 equal columns x4 equal rows, 24 full bodies row-major. Fixed camera, fixed zoom and body scale; place all torso centers and foot baselines at the guide's fixed positions. Keep a generous transparent margin around every whole figure, including horns/ahoge above and shoes below; no clipping or crossing into adjacent cells. Same head size, shoulder/waist size, short legs, hair and garment volumes in all frames. Only pose changes.
Motion is a gentle2-second thinking loop, at the EXACT progressive poses in guide:
1 neutral, hand low;
2 hand only slightly lifted, NOT near chin yet;
3 forearm halfway across low belly, NOT touching chin;
4 hand near lower chest;
5 hand near upper chest;
6 hand close below chin;
7 fingertips softly contact chin;8 tilted thinking hold;
9 BOTH eyes half close;10 BOTH eyes fully close;11 BOTH half open;12 BOTH open.
13-16 keep hand to chin with a visible but gentle4degree head tilt matching guide. Head and eyes MUST actually tilt, not just remain horizontal in all24 frames. Feet planted, torso upright. Tiny idle motion in the other hand, hanging sleeves, hair and tail.
17-24 steadily lower hand and straighten head using each specific guide pose, returning to exactly the relaxed beginning posture. The sequence must include distinct intermediate lifting/lowering poses rather than a jump from waist to chin. Both-eye blink, never a wink.
Background is ACTUAL clear transparent alpha0, with no floor, shadow, text, frame lines or checkerboard. Keep clean antialiased character edges and all fine painted details. NO standalone white or colored speckles. Stable face, costume, lighting, colors and proportion across every frame. Deliver ONLY the finished character atlas, not the guide.
